## Parsing (vendored in `parser/`)

Outline, completion, and Tier B formatting use a **local copy** of the tree-sitter web runtime and ABL grammar (MIT), not the `web-tree-sitter` or `tree-sitter-abl` npm packages at runtime:

- `parser/runtime/` — [tree-sitter/tree-sitter](https://github.com/tree-sitter/tree-sitter) **v0.24.7** `lib/binding_web` + `tree-sitter.wasm`.
- `parser/abl/` — [eglekaz/tree-sitter-abl](https://github.com/eglekaz/tree-sitter-abl) **0.1.2** (`grammar.js`, `src/scanner.c`, `tree-sitter-abl.wasm`).

`npm run build:parser` copies WASM into `src/assets/`. `npm run sync:parser-sources` refreshes vendored files from upstream pins.

## Grammar tests (dev only)

Unit tests load TextMate grammars with [vscode-textmate](https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-textmate) and [vscode-oniguruma](https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-oniguruma) (MIT License). These packages are devDependencies and are **not** shipped in the VSIX.

## ADE corpus (tests only)

Regression tests optionally use [progress/ADE](https://github.com/progress/ADE) at branch `release-12.8.x` (Apache License 2.0). The corpus is **not** shipped in the VSIX; it is checked out under `corpus/ade` locally or in CI.
